course: dictionary
lesson: 9752
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A dictionary gives each meaning its own number, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Read the words around the word and ask which meaning fits best.
explain: «Sam told his little cousin that eating a bug would give him a superpower.» Here a superpower is an amazing power beyond normal humans, like the powers of a superhero. Nobody gets real powers from eating a bug, so Sam is joking, but the meaning is still the superhero kind.
explain: «Counting is a superpower in biology.» This is a different meaning. Try the superhero meaning in the sentence: it does not make sense. Try a special talent instead: counting is a talent you are very good at, so that meaning fits.
fact: Superpower can mean a very powerful country with great military and economic strength that has a big influence over the world.
fact: Superpower can mean an amazing power beyond normal humans, like flying or being invisible, that a superhero has.
fact: Superpower can also mean a special talent or something you are very good at, as in «my superpower is…» (this is informal).
fact: «Binary search» is a superpower for finding things quickly: 8 cards need only 3 questions, and 16 books need only 4.
fact: Some real animals have amazing abilities too: the axolotl can regrow lost legs.
exercise: «Sam told his little cousin that eating a bug would give him a superpower.» What kind of superpower is this? | A powerful army | *An amazing power beyond normal humans | A country with great military strength | A talent for being good at maths
exercise: «Counting is a superpower in biology.» What does superpower mean here? | *A special talent or something you are very good at | An amazing power like flying | A very powerful country | A test you must pass
exercise: Which sentence uses superpower to mean a very powerful country? | Every superhero has a superpower | *Two world superpowers met to talk about peace | I can fly, and that is my superpower | My superpower is spelling
test: «Imagine unlocking the other ninety!» It feels like a secret superpower waiting inside your head. What does superpower mean here? | A tiny animal | A powerful country | A type of cape | *A special talent you may not know you have
test: Jayden says, «My superpower is remembering names.» What meaning is he using? | *A special talent or something you are very good at | An amazing power beyond normal humans | A very powerful country | A film about heroes
exam: In a history lesson the text says, «One superpower had great military strength.» What does superpower mean here? | A hero's cape | An amazing power beyond normal humans | *A very powerful country with great military and economic strength | A special talent
